From: Stamp-P4 maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] esp32_sdio: opt-in CMD53 PIO-write probe (#35)

es_reg_probe (0041) exercises the host read path; this battery
exercises the write path.  The P4 SDMMC BUFFIFO does not pop on CPU
reads, so a multi-word PIO read returns its first word repeated
(0085/0087); whether CPU *writes* push the FIFO correctly was never
isolated.  esp-hosted pads every TX write up to a word
(len_to_send = (len + 3) & ~3), so any packet that pads below the
16-byte DMA threshold - 8 and 12 byte writes in practice - still
goes out by programmed I/O.

Target-window model (verified on hardware):
the C6 SLCHOST window has no large inert scratch.

  * CONF_W7[0] (0x8c) is the esp-hosted host->slave interrupt
    vector.  A write of value v - by CMD52 *or* by CMD53 - raises
    slave slc0int bits v[7:0] and the slave event_cb runs once per
    set bit: bit0=open, bit1=close-data-path (-> esp_restart),
    bit2=reset (sdio_reset), bit3/4=power-save transitions.
    Verified: CMD52 of 0x02 reboots the C6 and drops the link;
    0x40 (bit6, unassigned) is ignored; a CMD53 write of 0xe9
    covering 0x8c fired bit3 (power-save) and silently wedged the
    data path while commands still answered.  es_wr_span_safe()
    therefore rejects every transfer that touches 0x8c, and the
    CMD52 restore pass never writes it.  CONF_W7[0] does not
    retain (always reads 0).
  * CONF_W0..6 (0x6c..0x8b, minus 0x84 WIN_CMD) and CONF_W7[1..3]
    (0x8d..0x8f) are shared storage with no doorbell semantics;
    verified by a CMD52 write of 0x02 to 0x8d leaving the link
    up.  CONF_W7 retains only odd byte lanes (0xefbeadde reads
    back 0x00be00de).
  * WIN_CMD (0x84) remaps the slave window; PKT_LEN0..2
    (0x90..0x9b) drive the slave packet accounting - a host write
    covering PKT_LEN1 wedges the SDIO function on either PIO or
    IDMAC until reset (measured); CHECK_SUM0/1, SLC1_TOKEN_RDATA
    and the 0xbc..0xc7 tail are RO; TOKEN_WDATA (0xc8) feeds
    buffer accounting.
  * CONF_W8..15 (0x9c..0xbb) raise no interrupt, but the running
    C6 republishes its observe sequence there (~4 Hz): a write
    lands but a republish can rewrite it before read-back, so
    those positions are reported as volatile deltas (vd) and
    never counted as mismatches.

es_wr_addr selects the incrementing battery base (default 0x88,
which only admits len<=8 under the span guard); 0x9c gives the
full 8..32 B coverage inside CONF_W8..15.  0x88..0xc7 is saved
over CMD52 before the battery; afterwards only CONF_W6
(0x88..0x8b) is restored, the single inert span that is both
provably safe to CMD52-write and worth restoring.

es_wr_probe is a bitmask, default 0 = fully off; writing it under
/sys/module/esp32_sdio/parameters re-runs the battery under one
sdio_claim_host, same as es_reg_probe.

Bits:
  0x01  incr-short  for len in {8,12,16,20,24,28,32} at es_wr_addr:
                    one write with an unaligned source buffer (forced
                    PIO at any len through the sg offset&3 gate) and
                    one with an aligned source (PIO for len<16 under
                    the default 16 B threshold, IDMAC otherwise);
                    each is followed by an IDMAC read-back (>=16 B
                    direct, <16 B via the fifo-no-pop bounce) and a
                    CMD52 oracle read; both compared, RO skipped,
                    CONF_W8..15 counted as vd.  Any span touching a
                    hazardous register (below 0x88, 0x8c, PKT_LEN,
                    >=0xbc) is skipped instead of issued.
  0x02  incr-long   len in {40,48,56,64} at 0x88: same two write
                    variants; inert coverage is the first 8 bytes.
  0x04  fixed       len in {40,48,56,64} fixed-address at 0x88
                    (sdio_writesb, OP=0): every byte lands on
                    CONF_W6[0], so the final byte proves how many
                    pushes the FIFO path really made; verified by
                    IDMAC read and CMD52.

Pattern: byte i of a write is seed + 7*i; the seed advances on
every transfer so stale window contents can never alias the
expected data.  A transfer the slave never saw still mismatches.

Residual: before the 0x8c guard, a battery at base 0x88 could
write a random pattern byte onto the doorbell; bits 1/2/4 (about
62% of byte values) restart or reset the slave mid-probe, bit3
leaves commands alive but wedges the data path.  Both failure
shapes were measured; with the guard the battery cannot touch the
vector at any base.  Production traffic never writes SLCHOST
registers - host TX goes to packet RAM - so this was a
probe-harness hazard, not a production-path defect.  A
post-battery liveness line and per-byte restore logging remain as
diagnostics.

--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -49,6 +49,11 @@
 static u32 es_reg_pattern;
 static struct sdio_func *es_probe_func;
 static void es_run_reg_probe(void);
+
+/* #35 write-side companion probe (opt-in, default off). */
+static u32 es_wr_probe;
+static u32 es_wr_addr = 0x88;	/* CONF_W6 & ESP_ADDRESS_MASK */
+static void es_run_wr_probe(void);
 static atomic_t tx_pending;
 static atomic_t queue_items[MAX_PRIORITY_QUEUES];
 struct task_struct *tx_thread;
@@ -1332,6 +1337,8 @@
 
 	if (es_reg_probe)
 		es_run_reg_probe();
+	if (es_wr_probe)
+		es_run_wr_probe();
 
 	esp_info("ESP SDIO probe completed\n");
 
@@ -1644,3 +1651,298 @@
 module_param_named(es_reg_pattern, es_reg_pattern, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(es_reg_pattern,
 		 "#35 debug: nonzero value CMD52-written before the battery");
+/* ===== #35 debug: opt-in CMD53 PIO-write probe battery =====
+ *
+ * es_reg_probe exercises the host read path; this battery exercises
+ * the write path.  On this board a CPU FIFO read does not pop the
+ * P4 BUFFIFO, so multi-word PIO reads return the first word
+ * repeated; whether CPU writes push correctly is what this probe
+ * answers.  Production writes take PIO whenever the padded length
+ * is below dw_mmc's 16-byte DMA threshold, i.e. every TX packet
+ * that pads to 4/8/12 bytes.
+ *
+ * Safe write target: the C6 SLCHOST window offers no large inert
+ * scratch.  CONF_W0..4 (0x6c..0x7f) are doorbells whose writes raise
+ * slave FRHOST bits 0..4 - on the running esp-hosted-ng firmware
+ * event_cb(0..4) means open/close-data-path, sdio_reset, and power
+ * save transitions, so they are off limits.  WIN_CMD (0x84) remaps
+ * the host-visible slave window.  TOKEN_WDATA (0xc8) feeds the
+ * buffer-accounting FIFO.  What remains: CONF_W5..7 (0x80..0x8f
+ * minus WIN_CMD) raise FRHOST bits 5..7, which event_cb passes to
+ * event_handler whose switch only covers 0..4, so they are no-ops;
+ * and CONF_W8..15 (0x9c..0xbb), which raise no interrupt at all but
+ * which the running C6 republishes with its ~4 Hz observe sequence
+ * (magic 0x0b23, byte 3 is a live counter).  The battery therefore
+ * bases every incrementing write at 0x88 (CONF_W6/7 = the only 8
+ * strictly inert bytes), skips read-only spans (PKT_LEN0..2,
+ * CHECK_SUM0/1, SLC1_TOKEN_RDATA) in the compare, and reports bytes
+ * landing on CONF_W8..15 as volatile deltas (vd) that a republish
+ * can legitimately flip - never counted as mismatches.  The span
+ * 0x88..0xc7 is saved over CMD52 first and restored after.
+ *
+ * CONF_W7 (0x8c..0x8f) quirk: the register only retains its odd
+ * byte lanes.  A CMD52 bytewise write of ef be ad de reads back
+ * 00 be 00 de, and a CMD53 write shows the identical pattern, so
+ * this is a slave register semantic, not a transport artifact;
+ * even-lane bytes are classed ES_WR_LANES and excluded from the
+ * compare like read-only positions.
+ *
+ * Measured hazard: a CMD53 byte-mode write whose span covers the
+ * slave's packet-length registers (PKT_LEN0..2, 0x90..0x9b; the
+ * wedge was observed after the first write reaching PKT_LEN1,
+ * 0x94..0x97) kills the SDIO function on both the PIO and the
+ * IDMAC transport - the write itself completes and the next
+ * command times out until the C6 is reset.  Production traffic
+ * writes packet RAM, never these registers, so the hazard is a
+ * probe-only concern; es_wr_span_safe() skips any transfer whose
+ * span touches PKT_LEN, the RO tail 0xbc..0xc7 or TOKEN_WDATA,
+ * so no base can take the link down.  Full coverage of the
+ * 16..64 B lengths therefore needs es_wr_addr=0x9c (the 32 B
+ * volatile window); at the 0x88 default only len<=8 runs.
+ *
+ * es_wr_probe bits:
+ *   0x01  incr-short  len in {8,12,16,20,24,28,32} at es_wr_addr
+ *   0x02  incr-long   len in {40,48,56,64} at 0x88
+ *   0x04  fixed       len in {40,48,56,64} fixed-address at 0x88
+ *                     (sdio_writesb, OP=0; every byte lands on
+ *                     CONF_W6[0], so the final byte proves the push
+ *                     count)
+ * Each length runs twice: "pio" uses an unaligned source buffer
+ * (sg offset&3 -> PIO at any length) and "dma" an aligned one
+ * (PIO below the 16 B threshold, IDMAC at or above it - so the
+ * >=16 B dma rows are the write-then-DMA-read-back control).
+ * Each incr write is verified by an IDMAC read-back (the
+ * fifo-no-pop bounce covers <16 B) plus a CMD52 oracle read.
+ */
+#define ES_WR_SKIP	0
+#define ES_WR_INERT	1	/* CONF_W6 + odd CONF_W7 lanes hold data */
+#define ES_WR_LANES	2	/* even CONF_W7 lanes never hold data */
+#define ES_WR_VOLATILE	3	/* CONF_W8..15: C6 republishes while we probe */
+
+static int es_wr_class(u32 a)
+{
+	if (a >= 0x9c && a <= 0xbb)
+		return ES_WR_VOLATILE;
+	if (a >= 0x88 && a <= 0x8b)
+		return ES_WR_INERT;
+	if (a >= 0x8c && a <= 0x8f)
+		return (a & 1) ? ES_WR_INERT : ES_WR_LANES;
+	return ES_WR_SKIP;
+}
+
+static u8 es_wr_seed = 0x23;
+
+static int es_wr_cmp(u32 addr, const u8 *exp, const u8 *got, int len,
+		     int *checked, int *vdelta)
+{
+	int i, bad = 0;
+
+	*checked = 0;
+	*vdelta = 0;
+	for (i = 0; i < len; i++) {
+		int cls = es_wr_class(addr + i);
+
+		if (cls == ES_WR_SKIP || cls == ES_WR_LANES)
+			continue;
+		(*checked)++;
+		if (got[i] == exp[i])
+			continue;
+		if (cls == ES_WR_VOLATILE)
+			(*vdelta)++;
+		else
+			bad++;
+	}
+	return bad;
+}
+
+/* A transfer may not cover CONF_W7[0] (0x8c, the esp-hosted
+ * host->slave doorbell: any write of v fires event_cb once per set
+ * bit - bit1 esp_restart, bit2 sdio_reset, bit3 power-save block,
+ * bit4 sdio_reset), PKT_LEN0..2 (0x90..0x9b), the RO tail
+ * 0xbc..0xc7 or TOKEN_WDATA (0xc8): PKT_LEN coverage wedges the
+ * SDIO function, the rest are at best ignored. */
+static int es_wr_span_safe(u32 addr, int len)
+{
+	u32 end = addr + len - 1;
+
+	if (addr < 0x88 || end >= 0xc8)
+		return 0;
+	if (addr <= 0x8c && end >= 0x8c)
+		return 0;
+	if (end >= 0x90 && addr <= 0x9b)
+		return 0;
+	if (end >= 0xbc)
+		return 0;
+	return 1;
+}
+
+static void es_wr_one(const char *tag, u32 addr, int len, int off)
+{
+	struct sdio_func *func = es_probe_func;
+	u8 wbuf[80] __aligned(8);
+	u8 rbuf[80] __aligned(8);
+	u8 gold[80];
+	const char *path;
+	int wret, rret = 0, cret = 0, i;
+	int ck1, ck2, vd1, vd2, dma_bad, c52_bad;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < len; i++)
+		wbuf[off + i] = (u8)(es_wr_seed + i * 7);
+	es_wr_seed += 0x1f;
+
+	path = (off || len < 16) ? "pio" : "dma";
+	if (!es_wr_span_safe(addr, len)) {
+		pr_info("esp32_sdio: ES_WRPROBE: %-4s path=%s addr=0x%05x len=%d SKIP unsafe span\n",
+			tag, path, addr, len);
+		return;
+	}
+	wret = sdio_memcpy_toio(func, addr, wbuf + off, len);
+
+	memset(rbuf, 0x5a, sizeof(rbuf));
+	rret = sdio_memcpy_fromio(func, rbuf, addr, len);
+	dma_bad = es_wr_cmp(addr, wbuf + off, rbuf, len, &ck1, &vd1);
+
+	memset(gold, 0x5a, sizeof(gold));
+	for (i = 0; i < len; i++)
+		gold[i] = sdio_readb(func, addr + i, &cret);
+	c52_bad = es_wr_cmp(addr, wbuf + off, gold, len, &ck2, &vd2);
+
+	pr_info("esp32_sdio: ES_WRPROBE: %-4s path=%s addr=0x%05x len=%d "
+		"wret=%d dma(ret=%d mm=%d/%d vd=%d) "
+		"c52(ret=%d mm=%d/%d vd=%d)%s\n",
+		tag, path, addr, len, wret, rret, dma_bad, ck1, vd1,
+		cret, c52_bad, ck2, vd2,
+		(dma_bad || c52_bad) ? " <-- MISMATCH" : "");
+	if (dma_bad || c52_bad || vd1 || vd2)
+		pr_info("esp32_sdio: ES_WRPROBE:      exp=%*phN dma=%*phN c52=%*phN\n",
+			len > 40 ? 40 : len, wbuf + off,
+			len > 40 ? 40 : len, rbuf,
+			len > 40 ? 40 : len, gold);
+}
+
+static void es_wr_fixed(const char *tag, u32 addr, int len, int off)
+{
+	struct sdio_func *func = es_probe_func;
+	u8 wbuf[80] __aligned(8);
+	u8 rbuf[16] __aligned(8);
+	const char *path;
+	int wret, rret, cret = 0, i, bad = 0;
+	u8 exp0, c52b0;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < len; i++)
+		wbuf[off + i] = (u8)(es_wr_seed + i * 7);
+	es_wr_seed += 0x1f;
+	exp0 = wbuf[off + len - 1];	/* last byte pushed wins */
+
+	path = (off || len < 16) ? "pio" : "dma";
+	if (!es_wr_span_safe(addr, 1)) {
+		pr_info("esp32_sdio: ES_WRPROBE: %-4s path=%s addr=0x%05x len=%d SKIP unsafe span\n",
+			tag, path, addr, len);
+		return;
+	}
+	wret = sdio_writesb(func, addr, wbuf + off, len);
+
+	memset(rbuf, 0x5a, sizeof(rbuf));
+	rret = sdio_memcpy_fromio(func, rbuf, addr, 4);
+	c52b0 = sdio_readb(func, addr, &cret);
+	if (rbuf[0] != exp0)
+		bad++;
+	if (c52b0 != exp0)
+		bad++;
+
+	pr_info("esp32_sdio: ES_WRPROBE: %-4s path=%s addr=0x%05x len=%d "
+		"wret=%d expect0=0x%02x dma(ret=%d b0=0x%02x) "
+		"c52(ret=%d b0=0x%02x)%s\n",
+		tag, path, addr, len, wret, exp0, rret, rbuf[0],
+		cret, c52b0, bad ? " <-- MISMATCH" : "");
+}
+
+static void es_run_wr_probe(void)
+{
+	struct sdio_func *func = es_probe_func;
+	static const u8 short_len[] = { 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32 };
+	static const u8 long_len[] = { 40, 48, 56, 64 };
+	u32 base = es_wr_addr & ESP_ADDRESS_MASK;
+	u8 save[64];
+	int i, ret = 0;
+
+	if (!func) {
+		pr_info("esp32_sdio: ES_WRPROBE: no SDIO function bound yet\n");
+		return;
+	}
+	/* a <=32 B write must stay inside 0x88..0xc7: below 0x88 is
+	 * WIN_CMD (0x84), above 0xc7 is TOKEN_WDATA (0xc8). */
+	if (base < 0x88 || base > 0xa6) {
+		pr_info("esp32_sdio: ES_WRPROBE: es_wr_addr 0x%x outside safe span 0x88..0xa6\n",
+			base);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	sdio_claim_host(func);
+
+	for (i = 0; i < 64; i++)
+		save[i] = sdio_readb(func, 0x88 + i, &ret);
+	pr_info("esp32_sdio: ES_WRPROBE: saved 0x88..0xc7, ret=%d\n", ret);
+
+	if (es_wr_probe & 0x01)
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(short_len); i++) {
+			es_wr_one("pio", base, short_len[i], 1);
+			es_wr_one("dma", base, short_len[i], 0);
+		}
+	if (es_wr_probe & 0x02)
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(long_len); i++) {
+			es_wr_one("pio", 0x88, long_len[i], 1);
+			es_wr_one("dma", 0x88, long_len[i], 0);
+		}
+	if (es_wr_probe & 0x04)
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(long_len); i++) {
+			es_wr_fixed("pio", 0x88, long_len[i], 1);
+			es_wr_fixed("dma", 0x88, long_len[i], 0);
+		}
+
+	/* Liveness check: separates a battery-induced slave crash from a
+	 * restore-write trigger. */
+	sdio_readb(func, 0x88, &ret);
+	pr_info("esp32_sdio: ES_WRPROBE: post-battery liveness ret=%d\n", ret);
+
+	/* Restore CONF_W6 only (0x88..0x8b).  0x8c = CONF_W7[0] is the
+	 * esp-hosted host->slave doorbell: a CMD52 write of v fires
+	 * event_cb once per set bit (bit1 = CLOSE_DATA_PATH ->
+	 * esp_restart), so it is never written here.  CONF_W7[1..3] keep
+	 * probe residue (harmless scratch), CONF_W8..15 republish
+	 * themselves ~4x a second. */
+	for (i = 0; i < 64; i++) {
+		if (es_wr_class(0x88 + i) != ES_WR_INERT)
+			continue;
+		sdio_writeb(func, save[i], 0x88 + i, &ret);
+		if (ret) {
+			pr_info("esp32_sdio: ES_WRPROBE: restore 0x%02x ret=%d\n",
+				0x88 + i, ret);
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+	pr_info("esp32_sdio: ES_WRPROBE: restored inert bytes, ret=%d\n", ret);
+
+	sdio_release_host(func);
+}
+
+static int es_wr_probe_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
+{
+	int ret = param_set_uint(val, kp);
+
+	if (!ret && es_wr_probe)
+		es_run_wr_probe();
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static const struct kernel_param_ops es_wr_probe_ops = {
+	.set = es_wr_probe_set,
+	.get = param_get_uint,
+};
+
+module_param_cb(es_wr_probe, &es_wr_probe_ops, &es_wr_probe, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(es_wr_probe,
+		 "#35 debug: CMD53 PIO-write probe bitmask (0=off)");
+module_param_named(es_wr_addr, es_wr_addr, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(es_wr_addr,
+		 "#35 debug: window base for es_wr_probe (0x88=CONF_W6)");
